# nspr -- Netscape Portable Runtime, packaged for exactly one reason: NSS
# requires it, and evolution-data-server requires NSS.
#
# The chain is worth stating because nothing here wants a portable runtime for
# its own sake: gnome-shell links libedataserver and libecal unconditionally
# (meson.build 72-73), e-d-s hard-requires NSS, and NSS hard-requires NSPR.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://archive.mozilla.org/pub/nspr/releases/v4.37/src/nspr-4.37.tar.gz
SRC_SHA256=5f9344ed0e31855bd38f88b33c9d9ab94f70ce547ef3213e488d1520f61840fa
SRC_DIR=nspr-4.37/nspr

# THE SOURCE ROOT IS NESTED. The tarball unpacks to nspr-4.37/ containing a
# further nspr/ directory, which is why SRC_DIR carries both components and why
# BLFS's own instructions open with `cd nspr`. Pointing at nspr-4.37 alone finds
# no configure.
#
# This recipe ships its own prepare.sh and build.sh, which is unusual; both
# reasons are recorded in those files. The short version: two source edits BLFS
# requires, and a configure flag that is ARCHITECTURE-CONDITIONAL.
